'' AN OVERLOAD'S DEFINITION IS NOT A SECOND DECLARATION IN THE INTERFACE: 'declare function
'' Pick overload' and its 'function Pick overload' are two symbols of one signature, and
'' both were written, which the importer refused as TKO0677. And A LIBRARY'S EXPORT KEEPS
'' ITS NAME: 'declare function Tick lib "kernel32" alias "GetTickCount"' was chain-mangled,
'' in the module and in the importer, and the link found no ACME::SYS2::GetTickCount. And A
'' MODULE'S GLOBAL OPERATOR IS NO MEMBER in an importer: 'operator len' there counted a
'' receiver and named v23len, where the module defined v13len.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -i tests/modules/src/overlib/libs tests/modules/src/overlib/app/main.bas -o tests/modules/overlib.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/modules/overlib.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 2-1-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  4 44
